{
  "title": "Goals vs. subagents: independent Tasks vs. a blocking parallel batch",
  "summary": "Current implementation, traced from source; not a proposed redesign. A Goal owns a foreground coordinator Task and private full child Tasks. start_task returns after launch, so the coordinator can continue working and later consume ordered events. use_subagents starts parallel SubagentRunner instances but awaits every result before returning to the caller. These mechanisms compose: a Goal child can itself call use_subagents when enabled. Both share the workspace; private conversation state is not filesystem isolation. Goal execution is always Act; subagents inherit the caller's mode. Inspect nodes and edges for context, lifecycle details, constraints, and code links.",
